Day 7 – Spring Cloud Config
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Create Config Repository
Created a separate GitHub repository for configuration.
Configuration is stored outside the microservices.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Create Config Server
Created a Spring Cloud Config Server.
Config Server runs on port 8888.
It reads configuration from the GitHub Config Repository.
GitHub Config Repo
        ↓
Config Server :8888
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Connect User Service
Added Spring Cloud Config Client dependency.
Connected User Service to Config Server.
User Service uses:
spring.config.import=optional:configserver:http://localhost:8888
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. User Service gets configuration
Used:
spring.application.name=user-service
Config Server identifies User Service and provides its configuration.
Verified using /users/config.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. Move real setting to Config Server
Moved : server.port=8081 
from User Service's application.properties 
to : USER-SERVICE-dev.properties
So the port is now controlled centrally.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. DEV and TEST configurations

Created:
USER-SERVICE-dev.properties
USER-SERVICE-test.properties

DEV:
Hello from DEV Config Server
TEST:
Hello from TEST Config Server

Changed:
spring.profiles.active=dev
to:
spring.profiles.active=test
and verified the different values.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. Config Server Failure Test
Stopped Config Server.
Started User Service.
User Service couldn't retrieve app.message.
Application failed because the required configuration was unavailable.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
8. Connect Order Service
Added Config Client dependency to Order Service.
Connected it to Config Server.
Created:
ORDER-SERVICE-dev.properties
ORDER-SERVICE-test.properties
Moved Order Service's port and user.service.base-url configuration to Config Server.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Final Architecture :
                 GitHub
            Config Repository
                   ↓
           Config Server :8888
              ↙          ↘
     User Service       Order Service
        :8081                :8082










